ATTRIBUTION — Adepthood "Candle & Ink" design language
=======================================================

This file records the provenance of Adepthood's design language so the IP
position is auditable in-repo (epic #798 / design-language-01).

Reference material (inspiration only, not copied)
-------------------------------------------------
- awesome-design-md — the "Claude" design-language Markdown entry was read as a
  reference for *how to structure* a token-and-provenance doc. License: MIT.
  No code, tokens, color values, type scale, or prose were copied from it; it
  informed the format of DESIGN.md only.

Clean-room stance
-----------------
- Palette: the warm grounds (`surface.*`, `ink.*`) are derived from Adepthood's
  own pre-existing `colors.paper` journal palette. The terracotta `accent.*` is
  derived from Adepthood's own `colors.tier.clear` (#be6e46), darkened to clear
  WCAG AA as text. No swatch in the design language is taken from any
  third-party product or brand palette. (`googleBrand` also lives in
  `tokens.ts`, but is not part of the language — see "Third-party marks".)
- Showcase palette (#826): `showcase.*`/`onShowcase.*` are an original warm-umber
  derivation of Adepthood's own warm ink (`colors.paper.ink`) — a brown umber,
  not navy and not Material's `#121212`. No third-party product/brand swatch.
- Marks: no Anthropic (or any other company's) name, logo, wordmark, or brand
  swatch is presented as Adepthood's own. "Candle & Ink" is an internal name
  for this language. The one third-party mark in the app is Google's, used
  under Google's own terms and recorded below.
- Fonts: no proprietary/commercial font files are bundled, self-hosted, or
  embedded (#800). Both faces are platform-system stacks — serif
  (`fonts.serif`: Georgia / system serif) and sans (`fonts.sans`: system UI /
  sans-serif). No commercial face is pulled off the user's machine via fallback
  stacks for brand parity. If an OFL/Apache face is ever bundled, its license
  file must be committed and listed here.

Third-party marks used under their owner's terms
------------------------------------------------
- Google "Sign in with Google" button. Google requires — does not merely
  suggest — that apps using their identity service render this button to
  their published branding guidelines
  (https://developers.google.com/identity/branding-guidelines), and prohibits
  a monochrome "G", a custom icon, and the standard "G" on any fill other
  than their three approved themes. Adepthood therefore reproduces:
    * the standard colour "Super G" mark, as vector paths matching the asset
      Google supplies in signin-assets.zip, unaltered in geometry or colour
      (`features/Auth/components/GoogleSignInButton.tsx`);
    * Google's approved light and dark button palettes, and their four logo
      colours (`googleBrand` in `tokens.ts`).
  These values are NOT part of Candle & Ink and are not Adepthood's own. They
  are used solely to draw Google's own sign-in button, are never applied to
  any other surface, and must not be tuned or harmonised with the warm
  palette. `features/Auth/components/__tests__/googleBranding.test.ts` pins
  every value against Google's published table so drift fails the build.
- Apple "Sign in with Apple" button. Rendered by Apple's own
  `AppleAuthenticationButton` component rather than reproduced, so no Apple
  mark or swatch is copied into this repo at all.

Summary: original palette, no proprietary fonts, and the only third-party
marks are Google's and Apple's sign-in buttons — each drawn to its owner's
mandatory guidelines and recorded above, neither presented as Adepthood's own.
The only other external input is the MIT-licensed reference doc, used for
format guidance only.
